IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr5-sch7`

-- TESTS for Schedule 7 (Consequential Amendments), the three inserted rules that stand alone: lines 3555-3564, 3682-3686, 3703-3711.
-- Expected values are written from the text.  Everything else in Schedule 7 is inert (reason 2) and has no test.

§ `Paragraph 3(2) -- section 226(7A) to (7D) of FSMA (lines 3555-3564)`

#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS TRUE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS TRUE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7B) the person is within the subsection` WITH `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a family member of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE, `the person has been identified by the respondent, in carrying on an activity to which the rules apply, as a known close associate of a politically exposed person` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` WITH `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` WITH `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` WITH `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a complaint of another kind: the list is not closed
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7C) the complaint is one to which the subsection applies` WITH `the complainant complains that the complainant has been incorrectly identified as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE, `the complaint relates to an act or omission of the respondent in consequence of the identification of the complainant as a person within subsection (7B)` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` WITH `the person is within subsection (7B)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` IS (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` WITH `the person is within subsection (7B)` IS (JUST FALSE), `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` IS (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` WITH `the person is within subsection (7B)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` IS NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7A) the rules must provide that the person is eligible in relation to the complaint` WITH `the person is within subsection (7B)` IS (JUST TRUE), `the complaint is one to which subsection (7C) applies` IS (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7D) the term has the meaning given in` `sch 7 para 3(2) politically exposed person` EQUALS "regulation 35(12)"
#ASSERT `sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7D) the term has the meaning given in` `sch 7 para 3(2) family member` EQUALS "regulation 35(12)"
#ASSERT `sch 7 para 3(2) s 226(7D) the term has the meaning given in` `sch 7 para 3(2) known close associate` EQUALS "regulation 35(12)"

§ `Paragraph 12 -- paragraph 2A of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents Order (lines 3682-3686)`

#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS TRUE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- unable to apply the measures of regulation 28 only
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS TRUE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- able to apply regulation 28's measures but, where relevant, unable to apply those of regulations 33 and 35 to 37 (FORK S7-F1)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS FALSE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- those regulations are not relevant, and the agent could apply regulation 28's measures: not within the exception
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS FALSE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the agent forwards accurate details: the exception is about not forwarding
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS TRUE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- able to apply every required measure
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 12 paragraph 2 of Schedule 3 to the Estate Agents (Undesirable Practices) (No 2) Order 1991 applies` WITH `the estate agent does not forward accurate details of the offer` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulation 28` IS FALSE, `regulations 33 and 35 to 37 are relevant in relation to the offeror` IS TRUE, `the estate agent is unable to apply the customer due diligence measures required by regulations 33 and 35 to 37 in relation to the offeror` IS FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 18 -- regulation 48(2) and (3) of the Open-Ended Investment Companies Regulations 2001 (lines 3703-3711)`

#ASSERT `sch 7 para 18(b) the relevant date` EQUALS (Date 26 6 2017)
-- paragraph (3): made before the relevant date and determined on or after it
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` WITH `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 8 2017)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` WITH `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 25 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 26 6 2017)) EQUALS TRUE
-- made on the relevant date itself: not 'before'
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` WITH `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 26 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 8 2017)) EQUALS FALSE
-- determined the day before the relevant date: not 'on or after'
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (3) the application was made before and determined on or after the relevant date` WITH `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 25 6 2017)) EQUALS FALSE
-- paragraph (2): authorised on or after the relevant date, not within paragraph (3): may not
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 26 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 27 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- authorised the day before the relevant date: paragraph (2) does not reach it, and paragraph (1) is outside the sources
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 25 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- authorised on or after the relevant date, but within paragraph (3): paragraph (2) is lifted
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the open-ended investment company may issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` WITH `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 8 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 8 2017)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the provision is void
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS TRUE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 26 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS TRUE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no provision purporting to authorise bearer shares: nothing is there to be void
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS FALSE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 1 2020), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 2 2020)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a company authorised the day before the relevant date: outside the date the text fixes, so paragraph (2) does not void the provision (FORK S7-F2)
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS TRUE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 25 6 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 5 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 5 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a company within paragraph (3): 'Paragraph (2) does not apply' is the text's no
#ASSERT (`sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the provision in the instrument of incorporation is void` WITH `a provision in the instrument of incorporation purports to authorise the company to issue bearer shares` IS TRUE, `the date on which the open-ended investment company was authorised` IS (Date 1 8 2017), `the date on which an application for an authorisation order was made in relation to the company` IS (Date 1 6 2017), `the date on which that application was determined` IS (Date 1 8 2017)) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `The prohibition in regulation 48(2) -- run, not asserted`

-- authorised in 2020: the prohibition arises and the company issues bearer shares at time 1, which is a breach
#TRACE `sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the prohibition on issuing bearer shares` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 2 2020) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 7 an open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date` DOES `sch 7 issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` AT 1
-- authorised in 2020: the prohibition arises and the company does nothing until time 5
#TRACE `sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the prohibition on issuing bearer shares` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 2 2020) AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 5
-- authorised the day before the relevant date: no prohibition arises, so nothing is breached
#TRACE `sch 7 para 18(c) paragraph (2) the prohibition on issuing bearer shares` (Date 25 6 2017) (Date 1 5 2017) (Date 1 5 2017) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 7 an open-ended investment company authorised on or after the relevant date` DOES `sch 7 issue bearer shares under paragraph (1)` AT 1
